--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SINGLE GOAL
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Validate the real Apple UI across macOS/iPad split navigation and iPhone tab
navigation, covering shared components and every page's loading/empty/error/
success/stale states with deterministic, network-free, auth-free fixtures.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
STEP 1 — INVENTORY & COVERAGE PLAN
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* XCUITest targets: iOS bundle TeslaSyncUITests; macOS bundle TeslaSync-macOSUITests.
  Pre-existing suites: AppLaunchUITests, AuthOnboardingUITests, LiveDataUITests,
  PushNotificationsUITests (the P9-0001 -uiTestAuthState/-uiTestLiveDemo/
  -uiTestPushDemo harness). 6 NEW suites added by this artifact (below).
* Route registry: real AppRouteParser (Sources/App). Deep-link/alias matrix
  exercised through it via the routing scenario (no fabricated routes).
* Page parity ledger: apps/parity/apple-ledger.json — 100 units in "done" state.
  All 100 are enumerated in UITestParityCatalog and driven through every state.
* Component identifiers: shared TS components in TeslaSync/shared-surfaces and
  Sources/Components categories ui / charts / data-display / feedback / forms /
  maps / motion — each rendered with stable accessibilityIdentifiers.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
STEP 2-4 — DELIVERABLES (fixture harness + UI tests, no real network/auth)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
App-side launch-arg fixture harness  (apps/apple/Sources/UITestHarness/):
  * UITestHarness.swift        — parses launch args into UITestHarness.Options;
                                 uiTestEnvironment() view modifier; scenario root.
      Launch args:
        -uiTestScenario component-gallery|page-state|routing
        -uiTestAuthState authenticated         (existing P9-0001 contract)
        -uiTestAppearance light|dark
        -uiTestDynamicType <category, e.g. accessibility5>
        -uiTestLocale <bcp47>
        -uiTestReduceMotion true|false
        -uiTestOffline true|false
        -uiTestDeepLink <url|path>
        -uiTestParityUnit <unit-id>
        -uiTestPageState loading|empty|error|success|stale|offline
        -uiTestRoutePath <path>
  * ComponentGalleryView.swift — real TS components per category, category tab bar.
  * PageStateHarnessView.swift — PageStateCatalogView (lists 100 units) +
                                 PageStateHarnessView drives LoadableState through
                                 loading / empty / error+retry / success /
                                 stale / offline using real feedback components.
  * UITestParityCatalog.swift  — 100 parity unit IDs + ParityUnit derivation.
  * RouteHarnessView.swift     — resolves paths/URLs via the real AppRouteParser.
  Integrated in Sources/TeslaSyncApp.swift (scenario branch + deep-link init) and
  Sources/App/AppShell.swift (shell.commandPalette accessibility anchor).
  Harness uses NO real network and NO real auth (fixtures only).

UI test suites  (apps/apple/Tests/UI/) — 34 tests total across 6 new suites:
  * UITestSupport.swift                 — launch helpers / shared assertions.
  * ComponentGalleryUITests.swift       — component states per category.
  * PageStateParityUITests.swift        — every page-parity state + error retry,
                                          across compact/regular idioms.
  * DeepLinkRoutingUITests.swift        — deep links, route aliases, notification
                                          routing.
  * RealShellNavigationUITests.swift    — auth/onboarding shell, split vs tab nav,
                                          search/command palette, settings changes.
  * AccessibilityDynamicTypeUITests.swift — VoiceOver labels, focus order,
                                          Dynamic Type (accessibility5) resilience,
                                          Reduce Motion, light/dark, accessible
                                          alternate summaries for charts/maps.

