    ROOT CAUSE (host capability, NOT a defect in the deliverable):
      * Host has 0 valid code-signing identities
        (security find-identity -v -p codesigning => "0 valid identities found").
      * TeslaSync-macOS + TeslaSyncWidgets-macOS carry restricted entitlements
        (aps-environment / associated-domains) whose Xcode build pre-check
        REQUIRES a development certificate (Attempt B).
      * macOS hosted UNIT tests pass (25778) because the bundle is injected
        in-process; macOS UI tests launch a SEPARATE runner that must establish
        an accessibility/automation connection to the app, which hangs under
        every signing strategy attempted (unsigned, ad-hoc, ad-hoc+stripped) —
        the macOS UI-automation runner capability is unavailable in this
        agent/session context (signing + cross-session automation).
      * This is the R5 signing limitation already documented by predecessor
        P9-0001, which scoped its macOS run to unit tests for the same reason.
      * The SAME 34 UI-test source files compile into the macOS UI bundle (the
        macOS UI bundle BUILDS); only on-host EXECUTION is blocked. The identical
        files run green on iOS iPhone AND iPad, so the test logic is verified.
      Per prompt: "log any unsupported destination as BLOCKED rather than
      silently skipping" / "STATUS=BLOCKED if required simulators/runner missing".

